Z||000000||DaveL||10-31-2000||01:46 PM||||I haven't been able to check the adjustment of the throttle valve cable on my 87 SE 2.5 DIS because I haven't been able to find anything on it. The adjuster is at the tranny end of the cable, and doesn't seem to correspond to the illustrations in the Hayne's Manual. I see that the cable comes apart near the tranny, and have had it partially apart, but haven't tried to make the adjustment.||||reg||5
Z||000001||TheFiero64||10-31-2000||05:10 PM||||I don't think there is an adjustment. I have been known to be wrong though so don't listen to me only. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Fieroboy1||10-31-2000||07:56 PM||||Are you talking about the throttle linkage to the throttle body or the detent/tranny downshift cable?  I know the detent doesn't adjust since i tried that once with my 87 SE.  You're right about that Haynes manual, it shows the older style 4cyl illustrations but not the newer DIS engine.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||10-31-2000||08:19 PM||||the tranny TV cable most definatly can be adjusted on the DIS motor. The process is about the same.<P>Press the button on the side of the adjuster. extract the cable sleeve about 1/8-1/4 inch. <P>Make sure the button looks the same when you let go as when you started. If it's sitting higher or slanted you pulled the sleeve out to far. push the button and let it back in a little.<P>Turn the idler pulley on the manifold untill the TBI reaches close to WOT. This take considerable force. DO NOT step on the pedal or turn the TBI shaft to make this adjustment. As you load up the cable the sleeve will ratchet into the tranny.<P>You won't be able to get the TBI quite to WOT. Not unless your a very hefty individual anyway.<P>To get to WOT push the adjuster button and let the cable sleeve got into the tranny a couple teeth at a time by hand. Try reaching WOT after each small adjustment. You should only need about 1/16 or so of aditional adjustment.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-31-2000).]||||reg||1
